## Final report — PRD v2 audit + fix

### Verdict: the app is PRD v2 compliant ✅

I audited every section of `KeepItBack_PRD_v2.md` against the code. This tree is a **Supabase Auth** build (the PRD's 2026-10-28 auth update supersedes its Clerk references), and it checks out end to end:

| PRD section | Status |
|---|---|
| §3 Auth — session restore, protected routes, sign-in/up, email OTP, recovery, honest errors | ✅ [AuthProvider.tsx](src/auth/AuthProvider.tsx), all `(auth)` screens, `auth/callback` handles both link + numeric-code flows |
| §4 Save — URL validation, canonical dedup, 23505 race handling, `source` truthfully set, "Saved" only after DB confirm | ✅ [items.ts](src/api/items.ts) `saveUrl` |
| §4 Home/Library/Search — real rows, real counts, debounced search via `search_saved_items` RPC + filters, honest empty states | ✅ |
| §4 Item details/notes/tags/collections — real CRUD, confirmations before destructive actions | ✅ `content/[id]`, `collections/*` |
| §5 Instagram DM linking — HMAC-hashed single-use 10-min codes, server-only `account_link_codes` (RLS enabled, no policies → client can never read hashes), signature-verified + idempotent webhook, IGSID-based matching | ✅ [linking.ts](supabase/functions/_shared/linking.ts), `link-code`, `instagram-webhook` fail closed (503/401) when unconfigured |
| §8 Migration — timestamped SQL, text `user_id` vs `auth.jwt()->>'sub'`, RLS on every table, safe `search_path`, no seeds | ✅ both files present, never executed by me |
| §9 Docs — `.env.example` has variable names only; README covers Supabase setup, manual SQL steps, Edge Function secrets + deploy, verification checklist | ✅ |

### The one gap found and fixed
`src/lib/sync.ts` had a complete offline save queue (`saveUrlWithOffline` + encrypted local store + background sync engine), but the save screen called `saveUrl` directly — so saving offline produced a raw database error instead of queueing. Now:

- **[app/save.tsx](app/save.tsx)** — `doSave` uses `saveUrlWithOffline`; offline saves route to the item screen showing pending state, and the sync engine pushes them when connectivity returns. Metadata is passed through unchanged so online saves keep their title/thumbnail enrichment.
- **[src/lib/sync.ts](src/lib/sync.ts)** — `saveUrlWithOffline` now accepts optional `LinkMetadata` (typed import) and forwards it to `saveUrl`.

### Gates
- `npx tsc --noEmit` — **0 errors**
- `npx expo lint` — **0 errors**

### Still configuration-dependent (not code gaps, honestly gated in-app)
- Instagram DM linking needs `LINK_CODE_SECRET` + Meta webhook secrets deployed (`npx supabase secrets set …`); until then the app shows its real "Not configured" state.
- SQL migrations must be run manually in the Supabase SQL Editor (I did not run them, per the PRD).
- Share-to-app requires a dev build (`npx expo run:android`), which you already tested — my earlier fix makes Instagram shares save reliably on Android cold start.

